From: Sobs <antohasobne@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 10:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] video: bareapp: OpenGL pictures copied by the GPU, read a
 frame later

SDL_BAREAPP_GL_ASYNC=1 (a game's game.ini [env]): at each swap the GPU
copies the picture into one of two renderbuffers, scaled to the size it
gets in bare_app's frame, with a fence; the copy made at the swap before
(finished by then) is read back and shown. The game's work on the next
frame overlaps the GPU's on this one instead of waiting for it in
glReadPixels, and a scaled picture costs no CPU; the picture is a frame
late. Mesa's panfrost reads pixel buffer objects back on the CPU too, so
those would not help. Desktop OpenGL reads GL_BGRA, bare_app's own
layout: a plain copy. Needs framebuffer blits and fences (OpenGL 3,
OpenGL ES 3); off by default.
---
--- a/src/video/bareapp/SDL_bareapp.h
+++ b/src/video/bareapp/SDL_bareapp.h
@@ -75,6 +75,10 @@
